THIRD-PARTY STANDARDS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software implements the two-exponential thermal model of the IEC
60076-7 loading guide, with the equation structure taken from a peer-reviewed,
open-access publication: M. A. Gonzalez-Cagigal, J. A. Rosendo-Macias and A. Gomez-Exposito, "Parameter Estimation for Hot-spot Thermal Model of Power Transformers Using Unscented Kalman Filters", J. Mod. Power Syst. Clean Energy 11(2), 634-642, 2023, doi:10.35833/MPCE.2022.000439 (open access, CC BY 4.0), eqs. (20)-(23).
IEC standards are copyrighted works of the International Electrotechnical
Commission and are NOT redistributed here. No clause text, table, or figure
from the standard is reproduced in this repository.

The cooling-class constants used by this software are engineering assumptions
and are UNVERIFIED against the standard. No standards-conformity claim is
made. Users requiring standards compliance must obtain their own licensed copy
from the IEC. See the provenance banner in
README.md and in corefield/iec60076_7.py.

Loading limits are deliberately NOT supplied by this software; the caller must
source them and record their provenance. See corefield/envelope.py.

